[38;5;10mx > 0 && y < 0[0m makes the C loop forever ([38;5;10my == 0[0m is never reached, so [38;5;10my--[0m runs past [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m — signed overflow, UB). Those inputs cannot be differentially executed at all, since the C never returns; they're recorded as [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m rows 12–13 and excluded by a [38;5;10mterminates()[0m predicate whose soundness is itself asserted. [38;5;10mx == INT_MAX, y == 0[0m terminates but emits ~2³¹ lines, so it's excluded for runtime and covered by bounded magnitudes instead.[0m[0m
